  _   0  1  2  3  4
  A   1  0  1  2  3
  C   2  1  1  1  2
  E   3  2  2  2  1
```

### How do you optimise space to two rows?

Each cell dp[i][j] depends only on three cells: dp[i-1][j-1] (diagonal), dp[i-1][j] (above), and dp[i][j-1] (left). This means each row depends only on the previous row. We can keep just two arrays and alternate between them.

```java
package com.bank.dsa;

public class EditDistanceSpaceOptimised {

    public static int editDistance(String a, String b) {
        int m = a.length(), n = b.length();
        // Use the shorter string as columns for minimal space
        if (m < n) return editDistance(b, a);

        int[] prev = new int[n + 1];
        int[] curr = new int[n + 1];

        for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) prev[j] = j;

        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            curr[0] = i;
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                if (a.charAt(i - 1) == b.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    curr[j] = prev[j - 1];
                } else {
                    curr[j] = 1 + Math.min(prev[j - 1], Math.min(prev[j], curr[j - 1]));
                }
            }
            int[] temp = prev;
            prev = curr;
            curr = temp;
        }
        return prev[n];
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(editDistance("RAJHES", "RAJESH"));  // 2
    }
}
```

