```

### How is edit distance different from longest common subsequence?

| Aspect | Edit Distance | Longest Common Subsequence |
|---|---|---|
| Goal | Minimise operations to transform A into B | Maximise the length of matching elements |
| Operations | Insert, delete, replace | No explicit operations, just matching |
| Table meaning | dp[i][j] = min edits | dp[i][j] = max common length |
| Match case | dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] | dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1 |
| Mismatch case | 1 + min of three neighbours | max of two neighbours |
| Relationship | edit distance = m + n - 2 * LCS when only insert and delete are allowed |

When the replace operation is removed (only insert and delete allowed), edit distance equals `m + n - 2 * LCS(A, B)`. This connection helps verify solutions.

### What are common mistakes?

The most frequent mistake is indexing. The DP table is (m+1) by (n+1) but the string characters are zero-indexed. When filling dp[i][j], you compare `a.charAt(i - 1)` with `b.charAt(j - 1)`, not `a.charAt(i)` with `b.charAt(j)`.

```java
// WRONG: off-by-one indexing
for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++)
    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++)
        if (a.charAt(i) == b.charAt(j))  // ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException when i == m
            dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1];

// CORRECT: use i-1 and j-1 for character access
for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++)
    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++)
        if (a.charAt(i - 1) == b.charAt(j - 1))
            dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1];
```

Another mistake is forgetting the border initialisation. Without `dp[i][0] = i` and `dp[0][j] = j`, the table starts with all zeros and produces incorrect results.

### What are edge cases?

When one string is empty, the edit distance is the length of the other string. When both strings are identical, the distance is zero. When one string is a single character, the distance is either the other string's length minus one (if the character appears in it) or the other string's length.

```java
package com.bank.dsa;

public class EditDistanceEdgeCases {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(EditDistanceBasic.editDistance("", "RAJESH"));    // 6
        System.out.println(EditDistanceBasic.editDistance("RAJESH", ""));    // 6
        System.out.println(EditDistanceBasic.editDistance("RAJESH", "RAJESH")); // 0
        System.out.println(EditDistanceBasic.editDistance("A", "ABCDE"));   // 4
    }
}
```

