### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer should know that weighted edit distance assigns different costs to different operations. In name matching, a substitution between phonetically similar characters (S and SH) might cost less than a substitution between unrelated characters. This produces a generalised Levenshtein distance.

The Damerau-Levenshtein variant adds transposition (swapping two adjacent characters) as a fourth operation, which catches common typing errors more accurately.

For very long strings, approximate algorithms or banded edit distance (computing only a diagonal band of width k around the main diagonal) reduce the time from O(m * n) to O(m * k) when you only care about distances below a threshold k.
